    "description": "Geode, Crystal & Mineral Specimen Collection Lot\nNatural & Polished Geological Specimens\nMulti-Piece Assortment, 9.4 lbs Total Weight\nA diverse collection of lapidary and geological specimens featuring natural geodes, polished bookend halves, druzy quartz plates, and mineral formations. The assortment highlights varied crystallization habits, quartz interiors, banded chalcedony agate rings, and crystalline clusters suitable for study, display, or lapidary crafting.\nIncludes 2 cut and polished display geode halves (one dyed blue agate, one natural grey banded agate)\nMultiple hollow quartz geodes with sparkling internal crystal druse\nSeveral druzy crystalline quartz plates and mineral clusters\nMetallic mineral cluster and bagged assortment of small crystal fragments and stones\nCombined specimen weight: approximately 9.4 lbs\nCondition:\nNatural geological specimens with rough matrix exteriors and naturally fractured surfaces. Polished faces on the two cut agate bookends are smooth with flat bases for freestanding tabletop display. Minor natural shedding of small crystal debris is typical of raw mineral geodes.\nNOTE\n: Unless otherwise indicated, this is a\nUSED\n, donated item/lot. We take every effort to document the condition and visible cosmetic damages, though we are not subject matter experts and items may contain unseen flaws or imperfections, such as cracks, crazing, bowing or separation.\nIf you have any questions regarding an item,\nplease reach out to us before placing your bid\n. If applicable, any testing for power or functionality, servicing or cleaning will be mentioned within the listing. Please assume items are untested, unserviced and presented as pictured otherwise.\nJEWELRY\n: Gemstones have been tested with Presidium Gemstone Tester. Precious metals are tested with a Thermo Scientific Niton DXL. Testing results are included in our listings where applicable. Gold JSP solution & rare earth magnets may also be used in testing. Gemstones may be natural or lab created. We identify gemstones to the best of our ability and testing equipment, but\nwe cannot guarantee specific gemstones\nif they look or test similar to other stones. Sterling Silver items may have very slight or localized magnetic properties due to rhodium plating, non-silver components such as pins or springs in clasps, or dependent on the metal the silver was alloyed with. Watch condition and functionality will be documented when possible. Watches may otherwise not be running, have internal issues or need additional cleaning.\nPlease Note\n: Certain jewelry items and lots may experience tangling from the sorting and shipping process.\nAS-IS\n: Listings are sold\nAS-IS with no refunds for condition or functionality\n. This includes, but is not limited to all electronic listings, all card lots, all jewelry lots and grab bags.\nIf you have any questions regarding an item,\nplease reach out to us before placing your bid\n.\nCOMBINED SHIPPING\n: All Jewelry items can not be combined with other any other items, including other Jewelry items without contacting customer service before payment. We reserve the right to approve or deny combination of items for shipment at our discretion.",
